# THE LFOS ON THE BEAT (0.17.10): playing, an LFO's cycle is the song's place, so it starts on the bar whatever came before (a rate turned,
# a tempo changed); the Rate knob goes in order of speed, with 1/4T, 1/8., 1/4. and 1/2. new
seed 0
wait 2500
expect playing 1
turn SELECT 3 100
wait 300
expect view 3
# Rate: the knob's place in speed order (all the way down: 1/16T, engine number 11; then 1/4T, 1/8., 1/4., 1/2.)
spin K1 -20
wait 100
expect par16 11
spin K1 4
wait 100
expect par16 12
spin K1 1
wait 100
expect par16 13
spin K1 2
wait 100
expect par16 14
spin K1 2
wait 100
expect par16 15
# a while at 1/2. (three beats: odd to the bar); then 1 bar: at once on the bar (the free-running LFO kept wherever the 1/2. left it)
wait 1700
spin K1 1
wait 100
expect par16 2
wait 37
expect lfobar 0
wait 411
expect lfobar 0
# the tempo changed: still on the bar
tap HOME
spin K1 9
wait 1300
expect lfobar 0
wait 253
expect lfobar 0
shot lfo_bar.png
